  "final_message": "Waiting for `npm test` to finish.\nWaiting for tests to finish.\nWaiting for `npm run typecheck` to finish.\nWaiting for `npm run arch` to finish.\nWaiting for `npm run arch` to finish.\nTo maintain backward compatibility with downstream consumer contracts (`analytics-ingest` requiring `placedAt` and `billing-service` requiring `totalCents`), [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w4/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L30) now includes both the new field names (`amountCents`, `createdAt`) and retains the existing fields (`totalCents`, `placedAt`).\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\n1. [**`src/core/events.ts`**](file:///C:/avg/w4/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L60):\n   - In [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w4/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L30), added `createdAt` and `amountCents` while keeping `placedAt` and `totalCents`.\n   - In [`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w4/r/src/core/events.ts#L46-L60), mapped `createdAt: order.placedAt`, `placedAt: order.placedAt`, `amountCents: total`, and `totalCents: total`.\n\n2. [**`test/app.test.ts`**](file:///C:/avg/w4/r/test/app.test.ts#L21-L55) & [**`test/adapters.test.ts`**](file:///C:/avg/w4/r/test/adapters.test.ts#L40-L55):\n   - Updated event assertions to verify both the new and retained fields.\n\nAll unit tests (`npm test`), dependency-cruiser checks (`npm run arch`), and TypeScript checks (`npm run typecheck`) pass cleanly.\n",
